# The build context for `docker build -f server/Dockerfile .`, run from the repository
# root because every COPY in the Dockerfile names a server/ path.
#
# An allowlist, not a list of exclusions. Almost all of this repository is the Mac app —
# Swift sources, a vendored SQLCipher, the Sparkle xcframework, and a .build/ that runs to
# gigabytes — and the image needs none of it. Excluding the app piece by piece would send
# whatever the next directory is to the daemon until somebody noticed; naming the three
# paths the Dockerfile copies cannot drift that way. A new COPY needs a line here too.
*
!server/pyproject.toml
!server/uv.lock
!server/src/

# Inside the allowed paths: nothing a local run leaves behind, and never configuration.
# A container takes its environment from the platform, and an .env baked into a layer is
# a credential shipped wherever the image goes.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.env
**/.env.*
